{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For a contract of length L starting in month s, does it cover exactly the L consecutive months s, s+1, ..., s+L-1 (so a 2-month contract can start in month 1, 2, or 3, and a 3-month contract can start in month 1 or 2), or are contracts only allowed to start in month 1?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the valid start months and coverage definition for contracts of varying lengths."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The mutual exclusion rule says a 4-month contract forbids a 1-month contract — does this exclusion apply only to the 4-month and 1-month contract types (so a 4-month contract can still be combined with 2-month and 3-month contracts), or does choosing a 4-month contract forbid all other contract types?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the scope of the mutual exclusion rule, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same constraint."
}

